{"unit":"11","questions":[{"q":"O is the center. Find the circumference of the circle. Leave the answer in terms of π.","options":["16π cm","8π cm","64π cm","32π cm"],"why":"Circumference = 2 × π × radius = 2 × π × 8 = 16π cm.","src":"Review Q20(a), p.256","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"8 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"O is the center. Find the circumference of the circle. Leave the answer in terms of π.","options":["14π cm","7π cm","49π cm","28π cm"],"why":"Circumference = 2 × π × radius = 2 × π × 7 = 14π cm.","src":"Review Q20(b), p.256","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"7 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"O is the center. Find the circumference of the circle. Leave the answer in terms of π.","options":["31π cm","62π cm","15.5π cm","961π cm"],"why":"Circumference = π × diameter = π × 31 = 31π cm.","src":"Review Q20(c), p.256","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[70,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[70,120],[250,120]],"s":"31 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"O is the center. Find the circumference of the circle. Leave the answer in terms of π.","options":["17π cm","8.5π cm","72.25π cm","34π cm"],"why":"Circumference = 2 × π × radius = 2 × π × 8.5 = 17π cm.","src":"Review Q20(d), p.256","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"8.5 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"Radius 42 cm. Find the circumference. (Take π ≈ 22/7.)","options":["264 cm","132 cm","5,544 cm","528 cm"],"why":"2 × 22/7 × 42: 84 ÷ 7 = 12, 22 × 12 = 264 cm.","src":"Review Q21(a), p.257","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#BBDEFB"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"42 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"Radius 35 m. Find the circumference. (Take π ≈ 22/7.)","options":["220 m","110 m","3,850 m","440 m"],"why":"2 × 22/7 × 35: 70 ÷ 7 = 10, 22 × 10 = 220 m.","src":"Review Q21(b), p.257","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"35 m","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"Radius 6 m. Find the area. (Take π ≈ 3.14.)","options":["113.04 m²","37.68 m²","18.84 m²","452.16 m²"],"why":"3.14 × 6 × 6 = 3.14 × 36 = 113.04 m².","src":"Review Q22(a), p.257","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFF59D"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"6 m","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"A semicircle has diameter 32 cm. Find its area. (Take π ≈ 3.14.)","options":["401.92 cm²","803.84 cm²","1,607.68 cm²","50.24 cm²"],"why":"Radius 16 cm: ½ × 3.14 × 16 × 16 = ½ × 803.84 = 401.92 cm².","src":"Review Q22(b), p.257","fig":null},{"q":"An acrylic sheet is 2 quarter circles (radius 5 cm) and a 12 cm by 5 cm rectangle. Perimeter? (Take π ≈ 3.14.)","options":["49.7 cm","39.7 cm","31.4 cm","44.7 cm"],"why":"The 2 quarter arcs make half a circle: ½ × 2 × 3.14 × 5 = 15.7 cm. Then 15.7 + 12 + 12 + 5 + 5 = 49.7 cm.","src":"Review Q23, p.258","fig":null},{"q":"A wire forms 2 semicircles and 2 quarter circles, each with diameter 10 cm. Length of wire? (Take π ≈ 3.14.)","options":["47.1 cm","31.4 cm","62.8 cm","94.2 cm"],"why":"2 semicircles + 2 quarter circles = 3 half circles: 3 × ½ × 3.14 × 10 = 47.1 cm.","src":"Review Q24, p.258","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 7 m. Circumference? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["44 m","22 m","154 m","88 m"],"why":"2 × 22/7 × 7 = 2 × 22 = 44 m.","src":"p.150","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 21 cm. Circumference? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["66 cm","33 cm","132 cm","1,386 cm"],"why":"21 ÷ 7 = 3, 22 × 3 = 66 cm.","src":"p.151","fig":null},{"q":"Semicircle, diameter 10 cm. Perimeter? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["25.7 cm","15.7 cm","31.4 cm","20.7 cm"],"why":"Arc 15.7 cm + diameter 10 cm = 25.7 cm.","src":"p.151","fig":null},{"q":"Quarter circle, radius 5 cm. Perimeter? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["17.85 cm","7.85 cm","12.85 cm","31.4 cm"],"why":"Arc 7.85 cm + 5 + 5 = 17.85 cm.","src":"p.152","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 40 cm. Circumference? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["251.2 cm","125.6 cm","5,024 cm","502.4 cm"],"why":"2 × 3.14 × 40 = 3.14 × 80 = 251.2 cm.","src":"Do and Learn (a), p.153","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 20.5 cm. Circumference? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["64.37 cm","128.74 cm","32.19 cm","41 cm"],"why":"3.14 × 20.5 = 64.37 cm.","src":"Do and Learn (b), p.153","fig":null},{"q":"Estimate the circumference of a circle with diameter 13 cm.","options":["About 39 cm","About 13 cm","About 26 cm","About 169 cm"],"why":"About 3 × the diameter: 3 × 13 = 39 cm.","src":"Exercise 1(c), p.154","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 8.4 cm. Circumference? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["52.8 cm","26.4 cm","221.76 cm","16.8 cm"],"why":"2 × 8.4 = 16.8, 16.8 ÷ 7 = 2.4, 22 × 2.4 = 52.8 cm.","src":"Exercise 2(b), p.155","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 18 cm. Circumference? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["56.52 cm","113.04 cm","28.26 cm","254.34 cm"],"why":"3.14 × 18 = 56.52 cm.","src":"Exercise 3(a), p.155","fig":null},{"q":"3 quarter circles of radius 21 cm plus 2 radii. Perimeter? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["141 cm","99 cm","132 cm","174 cm"],"why":"¾ × 132 = 99 cm, then 99 + 21 + 21 = 141 cm.","src":"Exercise 4(a), p.156","fig":null},{"q":"A coaster has diameter 6 cm. Area in terms of π?","options":["9π cm²","36π cm²","6π cm²","3π cm²"],"why":"Radius 3 cm: π × 3 × 3 = 9π cm².","src":"Do and Learn 1, p.162","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 14 cm. Area? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["616 cm²","88 cm²","308 cm²","1,232 cm²"],"why":"22/7 × 14 × 14: 14 ÷ 7 = 2, 22 × 2 × 14 = 616 cm².","src":"Do and Learn 2(a), p.162","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 42 m. Area? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["1,386 m²","5,544 m²","132 m²","693 m²"],"why":"Radius 21 m: 22/7 × 21 × 21 = 66 × 21 = 1,386 m².","src":"Do and Learn 2(b), p.162","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 18 cm. Area? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["1,017.36 cm²","113.04 cm²","254.34 cm²","56.52 cm²"],"why":"3.14 × 18 × 18 = 3.14 × 324 = 1,017.36 cm².","src":"Do and Learn 3(a), p.162","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 26 m. Area? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["530.66 m²","2,122.64 m²","81.64 m²","40.82 m²"],"why":"Radius 13 m: 3.14 × 13 × 13 = 530.66 m².","src":"Do and Learn 3(b), p.162","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 9.2 cm. Area in terms of π?","options":["84.64π cm²","18.4π cm²","9.2π cm²","42.32π cm²"],"why":"π × 9.2 × 9.2 = 84.64π cm².","src":"Exercise 1(b), p.163","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 38 m. Area in terms of π?","options":["361π m²","1,444π m²","38π m²","19π m²"],"why":"Radius 19 m: π × 19 × 19 = 361π m².","src":"Exercise 1(d), p.163","fig":null},{"q":"Radius 4 m. Area? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["50.24 m²","25.12 m²","12.56 m²","200.96 m²"],"why":"3.14 × 4 × 4 = 3.14 × 16 = 50.24 m².","src":"Exercise 3, p.164","fig":null},{"q":"Diameter 34 cm. Area? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["907.46 cm²","3,629.84 cm²","106.76 cm²","453.73 cm²"],"why":"Radius 17 cm: 3.14 × 17 × 17 = 3.14 × 289 = 907.46 cm².","src":"Exercise 4, p.164","fig":null},{"q":"Semicircle with diameter 28 cm. Area? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["308 cm²","616 cm²","1,232 cm²","44 cm²"],"why":"Radius 14 cm: ½ × 22/7 × 14 × 14 = ½ × 616 = 308 cm².","src":"Exercise 5(a), p.165","fig":null},{"q":"Quarter circle with radius 21 cm. Area? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["346.5 cm²","1,386 cm²","693 cm²","33 cm²"],"why":"¼ × 22/7 × 21 × 21 = ¼ × 1,386 = 346.5 cm².","src":"Exercise 5(b), p.165","fig":null},{"q":"A circular paper has diameter 14 cm. Area? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["153.86 cm²","615.44 cm²","43.96 cm²","21.98 cm²"],"why":"Radius 7 cm: 3.14 × 49 = 153.86 cm².","src":"p.166","fig":null},{"q":"A circular field has diameter 12.5 m. Circumference? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["39.25 m","78.5 m","122.66 m","19.63 m"],"why":"3.14 × 12.5 = 39.25 m.","src":"p.166","fig":null},{"q":"A semicircle (radius 10 cm) has a triangle (base 20 cm, height 10 cm) inside. Shaded area? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["57.14 cm²","157.14 cm²","100 cm²","214.29 cm²"],"why":"157.14 - 100 = 57.14 cm².","src":"Do and Learn 1, p.170","fig":null},{"q":"A table has radius 26.5 cm. Length of cloth around it? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["166.57 cm","83.29 cm","2,207.07 cm","53 cm"],"why":"2 × 22/7 × 26.5 = 1,166 ÷ 7 ≈ 166.57 cm.","src":"Exercise 1, p.171","fig":null},{"q":"A wheel of radius 25 cm makes 50 turns. Distance in meters? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["78.5 m","7,850 m","157 m","39.25 m"],"why":"1 turn = 157 cm. 50 × 157 = 7,850 cm = 78.5 m.","src":"Exercise 3, p.172","fig":null},{"q":"A wheel of diameter 49 cm rolls 924 cm. How many complete turns? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["6","154","19","3"],"why":"1 turn = 154 cm. 924 ÷ 154 = 6.","src":"Exercise 4, p.172","fig":null},{"q":"⅓ of a circle with radius 9 cm. Perimeter of that part? (π ≈ 3.14)","options":["36.84 cm","18.84 cm","56.52 cm","27.84 cm"],"why":"Arc = ⅓ × 56.52 = 18.84 cm, plus 9 + 9 = 36.84 cm.","src":"Exercise 5(a), p.173","fig":null},{"q":"A 28 cm square handkerchief with 8 semicircles of radius 7 cm. Area? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["1,400 cm²","784 cm²","2,016 cm²","1,092 cm²"],"why":"784 + 4 × 154 = 784 + 616 = 1,400 cm².","src":"Exercise 6, p.173","fig":null},{"q":"2 wheels (radius 7 cm) close 88 cm every 2 seconds and must cover 704 cm. Time? (π ≈ 22/7)","options":["16 seconds","8 seconds","32 seconds","4 seconds"],"why":"704 ÷ 88 = 8 turns, 8 × 2 = 16 seconds.","src":"Problem Solving, p.177","fig":null}]}